🚽 Test case: round-24 review finding #2, a second base type -- the
🚽 review specifically asked to test `chad *`/`skibidi *` too, since
🚽 pointer width can coincidentally match one scalar width and not
🚽 another's across native/wasm32. `chad *` (float, always 4 bytes)
🚽 exercises a different scalar width than the int-array fixture.
skibidi main {
    chad a = 1.5;
    chad b = 2.5;
    chad *ptrs[2] = { &a, &b };
    yappin("%.1f %.1f\n", *ptrs[0], *ptrs[1]);
    *ptrs[1] = 9.5;
    yappin("%.1f %.1f\n", a, b);
    bussin 0;
}
